{"id": "845b9a98-afab-41f6-81fa-fdf56545431b", "card": {"foregroundColor": {"blue": 1, "green": 1, "opacity": 1, "red": 1}, "image": "", "imageStyle": "textFirst", "localizedTitle": {"en": "### Yellowstone Volcano", "es": "### El volc\u00e1n de Yellowstone", "pt": "### O Vulc\u00e3o de Yellowstone"}}, "pages": [{"id": "6b6f6f27-7183-4448-96d4-d8ac2eff0040", "blocks": [{"id": "376e5fcb-0aa9-4626-88b4-e07c27737d57", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Volcanoes and Earthquakes", "es": "## Volcanes y terremotos", "pt": "## Vulc\u00f5es e Terremotos"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "c6dc0e08-cd78-40f5-b2a9-8e18e02ca40f", "height": "regular", "image": "", "type": "image"}, {"id": "d5f06489-662b-4ba0-8b78-af5f4c08040e", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Yellowstone is an area known for its geothermal features like geysers,\nhotspots, and of course, for representing one of the Earth's most explosive\nsupervolcanoes. In addition to its geothermal landscape, Yellowstone contains\na series of fault lines and is seismically active. **There are thousands earthquakes\nwithin Yellowstone National Park** boundaries annually, most of which are\nso small in magnitude that only sensitive instruments can detect the seismic\nwaves. The data from these small earthquakes are often used as proxies to\nmap out the shape of the volcano's caldera and monitor the movement of magma\nbeneath the Earth's surface.\n", "es": "Yellowstone es un \u00e1rea conocida por sus caracter\u00edsticas geot\u00e9rmicas como\ng\u00e9iseres, puntos calientes y, por supuesto, por representar uno de los supervolcanes\nm\u00e1s explosivos de la Tierra. Adem\u00e1s de su paisaje geot\u00e9rmico, Yellowstone\ncontiene una serie de fallas y es s\u00edsmicamente activo. **Hay miles de terremotos\ndentro de los l\u00edmites del Parque Nacional de Yellowstone** anualmente. La\nmayor\u00eda son de una magnitud tan peque\u00f1a que solo con instrumentos sensibles\nse pueden detectar las ondas s\u00edsmicas. Los datos de estos peque\u00f1os terremotos\nse utilizan a menudo como sustitutos para trazar la forma de la caldera del\nvolc\u00e1n y monitorear el movimiento del magma debajo de la superficie de la\nTierra.\n", "pt": "Yellowstone \u00e9 uma \u00e1rea conhecida por suas fei\u00e7\u00f5es geot\u00e9rmicas, como g\u00eaiseres, pontos\nquentes e, claro, por abrigar um dos supervulc\u00f5es mais explosivos do planeta.\nAl\u00e9m da paisagem geot\u00e9rmica, Yellowstone possui v\u00e1rias falhas e \u00e9 s\u00edsmicamente\nativo. **Todos os anos ocorrem milhares de terremotos dentro dos limites do\nParque Nacional de Yellowstone**, a maioria t\u00e3o pequena que apenas instrumentos\nsens\u00edveis conseguem detectar as ondas s\u00edsmicas. Os dados desses pequenos abalos\ns\u00e3o usados como proxy para mapear o formato da caldeira do vulc\u00e3o e monitorar\no movimento do magma sob a superf\u00edcie terrestre.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "b75e8eaf-7669-4d21-af23-614e47fabef2", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}, {"id": "981a905d-935d-4ab5-a621-0cb534f8c00f", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "> **Note:** NASA Earth Observatory images by Joshua Stevens, using Landsat\ndata from the U.S. Geological Survey and ASTER GDEM data from NASA/GSFC/METI/ERSDAC/JAROS,\nand U.S./Japan ASTER Science Team. Photograph courtesy of the National Park\nService. Caption by Mike Carlowicz.\n", "es": "> **Nota:** NASA Earth Observatory images by Joshua Stevens, using Landsat\ndata from the U.S. Geological Survey and ASTER GDEM data from NASA/GSFC/METI/ERSDAC/JAROS,\nand U.S./Japan ASTER Science Team. Photograph courtesy of the National Park\nService. Caption by Mike Carlowicz.\n", "pt": "> **Observa\u00e7\u00e3o:** Imagens da NASA Earth Observatory por Joshua Stevens, usando\ndados Landsat do U.S. Geological Survey e dados ASTER GDEM da NASA/GSFC/METI/ERSDAC/JAROS,\ne da equipe cient\u00edfica ASTER EUA/Jap\u00e3o. Fotografia cortesia do National Park\nService. Legenda por Mike Carlowicz.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}], "title": "Page 1. Volcanoes and Earthquakes"}, {"id": "0ef8797e-5767-4b29-9268-4fdc9d3f1183", "blocks": [{"id": "ce2e7dc1-a70c-4d3d-b66b-89d2c625b791", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Tremors and Volcanoes", "es": "## Temblores y volcanes", "pt": "## Tremores e Vulc\u00f5es"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "75ada4eb-49e7-4fc8-b445-01541e334d45", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Distant earthquakes sometimes trigger local seismic activity in a region\nthat is seismically active. The two recordings below represent seismic data\ncollected from a **magnitude 7.4 earthquake near Ometepec, Mexico** on March\n20, 2012. One seismic station is **located in Yellowstone**, a seismically\nactive area. The other seismic station is located in **Red Lodge, Montana**,\nan area just outside of Yellowstone with lower seismic, volcanic, and geothermal\nactivity in comparison to Yellowstone.\n", "es": "A veces, los terremotos distantes desencadenan actividad s\u00edsmica local en\nuna regi\u00f3n que es s\u00edsmicamente activa. Los dos registros que vienen a continuaci\u00f3n\nrepresentan datos s\u00edsmicos recolectados de un mismo terremoto de **magnitud\n7.4 cerca de Ometepec, M\u00e9xico** registrado el 20 de Marzo de 2012. Una estaci\u00f3n\ns\u00edsmica est\u00e1 **ubicada en Yellowstone**, un \u00e1rea s\u00edsmicamente activa. La otra\nestaci\u00f3n s\u00edsmica est\u00e1 ubicada en **Red Lodge, Montana**, un \u00e1rea en las afueras\nde Yellowstone con menor actividad s\u00edsmica, volc\u00e1nica y geot\u00e9rmica en comparaci\u00f3n\ncon Yellowstone.\n", "pt": "Terremotos distantes \u00e0s vezes desencadeiam atividade s\u00edsmica local em regi\u00f5es\nj\u00e1 ativas. As duas grava\u00e7\u00f5es a seguir mostram dados s\u00edsmicos de um **terremoto\nde magnitude\u202f7,4 perto de Ometepec, no M\u00e9xico**, em 20 de mar\u00e7o de 2012. Uma\nesta\u00e7\u00e3o s\u00edsmica est\u00e1 localizada **em Yellowstone**, \u00e1rea altamente ativa; a outra est\u00e1 localizada em\n**Red Lodge, Montana**, fora do parque, onde h\u00e1 menor atividade s\u00edsmica, vulc\u00e2nica\ne geot\u00e9rmica em compara\u00e7\u00e3o a Yellowstone.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "4ae28741-03df-4cc5-8183-1896b5c4a362", "height": "huge", "image": "", "type": "image"}, {"id": "476aa34b-8530-48e0-98b9-bf546393fe5f", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}, {"id": "f026933a-10a6-4ebf-aa65-a9afa4041469", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "> **Note:** Screenshot from https://usgs.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html", "es": "> **Nota:** Captura de pantalla de https://usgs.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html", "pt": "> **Observa\u00e7\u00e3o:** Captura de tela de https://usgs.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}], "title": "Page 2. Tremors and Volcanoes"}, {"id": "9dff1910-caf3-47b1-86e0-bf1dfeac12d7", "blocks": [{"id": "526df963-68d4-49e3-8a85-b46b69cc6f84", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Questions", "es": "## Preguntas", "pt": "## Perguntas"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "c1b5b3b4-5680-4a9a-b2c0-ce0469598170", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Now, listen to the seismic data from each station location below. Do not\nonly pay attention to the sounds of the M7.4 earthquake, but also notice how\nthe sound compares in the seconds following the earthquake signals.\n", "es": "Ahora, escucha los siguientes datos s\u00edsmicos de la ubicaci\u00f3n de cada estaci\u00f3n.\nPresta atenci\u00f3n a los sonidos del terremoto M7.4 y realiza tambi\u00e9n una comparaci\u00f3n\ndel sonido de los segundos posteriores a las se\u00f1ales del terremoto.\n", "pt": "Agora, ou\u00e7a os dados s\u00edsmicos de cada esta\u00e7\u00e3o abaixo. N\u00e3o preste aten\u00e7\u00e3o\napenas aos sons do terremoto M7.4; repare tamb\u00e9m como o som se comporta nos\nsegundos que se seguem \u00e0s ondas s\u00edsmicas.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "44867096-1cb4-41e4-a06e-7239cb174e27", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Yellowstone**", "es": "**Yellowstone**", "pt": "**Yellowstone**"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "3acbe397-d455-4a42-8c20-b128b19782b8", "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 28800, "startDate": "2012-03-20T17:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "630C6D01-1737-45D3-AD3E-E22800BEB2EC", "name": "Yellowstone", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "--", "network": "TA", "station": "H17A"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "8d10ed4c-5b5c-44f4-af23-91d2be0c2137", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Red Lodge**", "es": "**Red Lodge**", "pt": "**Red Lodge**"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "c0576faf-0d4d-40ad-bd71-9749b397cfb2", "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 28800, "startDate": "2012-03-20T17:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "1BAB3528-487D-4E72-8548-3EA9215789BA", "name": "Red Lodge", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "00", "network": "US", "station": "RLMT"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "640c58b4-d925-48d4-b951-d4aa41b58215", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 1.** How is the sound that follows the strong M7.4 earthquake signals different\nin Yellowstone, Wyoming from that in Red Lodge, Montana?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 1.** \u00bfEn qu\u00e9 se diferencia el sonido que sigue a las fuertes se\u00f1ales del terremoto\nM7.4, registrado en Yellowstone, Wyoming del que se registr\u00f3 en Red Lodge,\nMontana?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 1.** Como o som que se segue \u00e0s fortes ondas do terremoto M7.4\ndifere em Yellowstone (Wyoming) em compara\u00e7\u00e3o a Red Lodge (Montana)?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "3f5ae0f1-6f31-40f1-9686-4c98171b6031", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "In the time leading up to the seismic waves from the M7.4 earthquake arriving,\nthe Yellowstone station seems slightly quieter than the Red Lodge station.\nBut after the big seismic waves passed, the sound at Yellowstone seems a bit\nnoisier than that at Red Lodge.\n", "es": "Antes de la llegada de las ondas s\u00edsmicas del terremoto de magnitud 7.4,\nla estaci\u00f3n de Yellowstone parece estar un poco m\u00e1s tranquila que la estaci\u00f3n\nde Red Lodge. Pero despu\u00e9s de que pasaron las grandes ondas s\u00edsmicas, el sonido\nen Yellowstone parece ser un poco m\u00e1s ruidoso que en Red Lodge.\n", "pt": "Antes da chegada das ondas s\u00edsmicas do terremoto de magnitude 7.4, a esta\u00e7\u00e3o de Yellowstone parece\num pouco mais silenciosa que a de Red Lodge. Depois que as ondas principais\npassam, por\u00e9m, Yellowstone soa um pouco mais ruidosa do que Red Lodge.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "4d152db2-2950-4f0c-a65b-88524bc72534", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 2.** Could the local geology of each area, as described above, be a possible reason\nfor differences in sound you might have heard? And if so, how?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 2.** \u00bfPodr\u00eda la geolog\u00eda local de cada \u00e1rea, como se describi\u00f3 anteriormente, ser\nuna posible raz\u00f3n para las diferencias en el sonido que pudiste haber escuchado?\nY si es as\u00ed, \u00bfc\u00f3mo?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 2.** A geologia local de cada \u00e1rea, conforme descrito acima, poderia ser uma\nraz\u00e3o para as diferen\u00e7as de som que voc\u00ea percebeu? Se sim, como?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "40545f97-9758-4677-95a7-9a977aa551c2", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "Yellowstone is seismically, hydrothermally, and volcanically active, suggesting it is in a state of ongoing change while Red Lodge is in a stiff part of North America that has not deformed for at least a billion years. This might make the Red Lodge area less susceptible to ongoing activity or slow adjustment after the main seismic waves from the M7.4 passed.", "es": "Yellowstone es s\u00edsmica, hidrotermal y volc\u00e1nicamente activo, lo que sugiere que est\u00e1 en un estado de cambio continuo, mientras que Red Lodge se encuentra en una parte r\u00edgida de Am\u00e9rica del Norte que no se ha deformado durante al menos mil millones de a\u00f1os. Esto podr\u00eda hacer que el \u00e1rea de Red Lodge sea menos susceptible a la actividad continua o a un ajuste lento despu\u00e9s de que pasaran las ondas s\u00edsmicas principales del terremoto de magnitud 7.4.", "pt": "Yellowstone \u00e9 uma \u00e1rea s\u00edsmica, hidrotermal e vulcanicamente ativa, indicando um estado de mudan\u00e7a cont\u00ednua, enquanto Red Lodge se situa numa parte r\u00edgida da Am\u00e9rica do Norte que n\u00e3o se deforma h\u00e1 pelo menos um bilh\u00e3o de anos. Isso pode tornar Red Lodge menos suscet\u00edvel a atividades cont\u00ednua ou a ajustes lentos ap\u00f3s a passagem das ondas principais do terremoto de magnitude 7.4."}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "02f2429a-3ebe-4d1c-8440-7d27ac83a13e", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 3.** Now click on the signal button at the bottom left-hand side of the audio track\nuntil it turns purple. This button, when selected, will auto-adjust the volume\nso that the seismic signal is not clipped (maxed out). Your record now sounds\ndifferently - can you explain how and why?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 3.** Ahora haz clic en el bot\u00f3n de se\u00f1al en la parte inferior izquierda de la onda\nhasta que se vuelva violeta. Este bot\u00f3n, cuando se selecciona, autoajustar\u00e1\nel volumen para que la se\u00f1al s\u00edsmica no se corte (sature). Ahora suena diferente,\n\u00bfpuedes explicar c\u00f3mo y por qu\u00e9?'\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 3.** Clique no bot\u00e3o de sinal no canto inferior esquerdo da faixa\nat\u00e9 que ele fique roxo. Selecionado, esse bot\u00e3o ajusta o volume automaticamente\npara que a onda s\u00edsmica n\u00e3o seja \"cortada\" (saturada). O registro soa diferente\nagora \u2014 voc\u00ea consegue explicar como e por qu\u00ea?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "82680d67-641d-44a8-813a-09b602d198ed", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "The volume was adjusted downwards to capture the largest seismic wave at maximum volume rather than clipping and distorting it when the seismic wave amplitude exceeds the maximum volume, so everything else sounds much softer now. The main seismic waves from the M7.4 earthquake are rich in low frequencies and sound much clearer when you increase the pitch by a few octaves!", "es": "El volumen se redujo para capturar la onda s\u00edsmica m\u00e1s grande a su volumen m\u00e1ximo en lugar de cortarla y distorsionarla cuando la amplitud de la onda s\u00edsmica excediese el volumen m\u00e1ximo, por lo que el resto suena mucho m\u00e1s suave. Las ondas s\u00edsmicas principales del terremoto de magnitud 7.4 son ricas en frecuencias bajas y \u00a1suenan mucho m\u00e1s claras cuando aumentas el tono por unas pocas octavas!", "pt": "O volume foi reduzido para registrar a maior onda s\u00edsmica no volume m\u00e1ximo, evitando \"cortes\" e distor\u00e7\u00f5es quando a amplitude ultrapassa o limite. Por isso, todo o restante soa bem mais baixo agora. As ondas principais do terremoto de magnitude 7.4 s\u00e3o ricas em baixas frequ\u00eancias e soam muito mais n\u00edtidas quando voc\u00ea aumenta o tom algumas oitavas!"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false, "unveil": {"unveilText": {"en": "Unveil answer", "es": "Desvelar respuesta", "pt": "Revelar resposta"}, "waitingTime": 5}}, {"id": "24fa647c-00c9-420f-b58a-018cedff3d20", "action": "close", "localizedText": {"en": "Close", "es": "Cerrar", "pt": "Fechar"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}, {"id": "039b1284-c7df-4088-a490-872264d2c40a", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "To learn more about Earthquakes at Yellowstone National Parks, Visit [nps.gov/yell/learn/nature/earthquakes.htm](nps.gov/yell/learn/nature/earthquakes.htm)\n", "es": "Para obtener m\u00e1s informaci\u00f3n sobre los terremotos en los parques nacionales\nde Yellowstone, visite [nps.gov/yell/learn/nature/earthquakes.htm](nps.gov/yell/learn/nature/earthquakes.htm)\n", "pt": "Para saber mais sobre terremotos nos parques nacionais de Yellowstone, visite\n[nps.gov/yell/learn/nature/earthquakes.htm](nps.gov/yell/learn/nature/earthquakes.htm)\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}], "title": "Page 3. Questions"}], "title": {"en": "Yellowstone Volcano", "es": "El volc\u00e1n de Yellowstone", "pt": "Vulc\u00e3o de Yellowstone"}}